\begin_layout Abstract
QUICHOTTE computes the spin-resolved current–voltage characteristics of a helical molecule with spin–orbit coupling (SOC) and an on-site Hubbard interaction,
 coupled to two leads.
 It uses self-consistent non-equilibrium Green's functions (NEGF),
 with the interaction treated to zeroth,
 first (Hartree–Fock) or second order in
\begin_inset space ~
\end_inset


\begin_inset Formula $U$
\end_inset

.
 The code was written to study chirality-induced spin selectivity (CISS).
 The Hamiltonian can be a model helix or a multi-orbital Hamiltonian with spin–orbit coupling from DFTB+
 (s and p orbitals on every atom),
 in which every spatial orbital is a Hubbard site;
 only the interacting and contact orbitals are stored.
 This manual gives the model,
 the equations the code solves,
 the numerical methods,
 a complete reference for the input and output files,
 and the practical workflow.
 The companion code 
\emph on
SANCHO
\emph default
 (in 
\begin_inset Flex Code
status collapsed

\begin_layout Plain Layout
SANCHO/
\end_layout

\end_inset

) treats a spinless chain to third order in
\begin_inset space ~
\end_inset


\begin_inset Formula $U$
\end_inset

 and has its own manual.
 
\end_layout

