\begin_layout Paragraph
Choosing the numerical parameters.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize
\begin_inset Flex Code
status collapsed

\begin_layout Plain Layout
delta
\end_layout

\end_inset

 must resolve the narrowest feature of the spectral function,
 whose width is set by 
\begin_inset Formula $\Gamma$
\end_inset

 and 
\begin_inset Formula $U$
\end_inset

.
 Halve it and compare.
 
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize
\begin_inset Flex Code
status collapsed

\begin_layout Plain Layout
dw
\end_layout

\end_inset

,
 
\begin_inset Flex Code
status collapsed

\begin_layout Plain Layout
up
\end_layout

\end_inset

 must contain the broadened spectrum;
 check that 
\begin_inset Formula $W_{a}\approx1$
\end_inset

.
 
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize
Runtime and memory grow as 
\begin_inset Formula $N_{\omega}\propto(\text{bandwidth}+\code{dw}+\code{up})/\delta$
\end_inset

, and at order 2 as 
\begin_inset Formula $n_{A}^{2}$
\end_inset

 (Section 
\begin_inset CommandInset ref
LatexCommand ref
reference "sec:active"
plural "false"
caps "false"
noprefix "false"
nolink "false"

\end_inset

). The Broyden history needs 
\begin_inset Formula $2\,\code{nhist}\cdot n$
\end_inset

 numbers (single precision by default), with 
\begin_inset Formula $n\approx3n_{A}^{2}N_{\omega}$
\end_inset

 at order 2 and 8 per interacting orbital at order 1. DFTB spectra are wide (about 50 eV for hexahelicene) and have narrow levels: keep 
\begin_inset Formula $\delta$
\end_inset

 small and put 
\begin_inset Formula $U$
\end_inset

 only where it matters.
\end_layout


\begin_layout Itemize
If a voltage does not converge,
 lower 
\begin_inset Flex Code
status collapsed

\begin_layout Plain Layout
alpha_mix
\end_layout

\end_inset

 (e.g.
\begin_inset space \space{}
\end_inset

0.2) or raise 
\begin_inset Flex Code
status collapsed

\begin_layout Plain Layout
maxscf
\end_layout

\end_inset

;
 large 
\begin_inset Formula $U/|t|$
\end_inset

 needs smaller 
\begin_inset Formula $\alpha$
\end_inset

.
 
\end_layout

