\begin_layout Standard
The restructured code reproduces the previous version (
\begin_inset Flex Code
status collapsed

\begin_layout Plain Layout
SCF_stype
\end_layout

\end_inset

) to better than 
\begin_inset Formula $3\times10^{-8}$
\end_inset

 in all currents,
 populations and 
\begin_inset Formula $\langle S_{z}\rangle$
\end_inset

 for orders 0–2 (October 2026).
 Before the clean-up,
 according to its commit history,
 the code agreed with the spinless code and with earlier independent implementations,
 gave 
\begin_inset Formula $J=0$
\end_inset

 at 
\begin_inset Formula $V=0$
\end_inset

,
 and satisfied 
\begin_inset Formula $\Gg=\Gl+\Gr-\Ga$
\end_inset

 with interactions.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
The active-subspace version (November 2026) reproduces the full-storage version: order-2 SCF histories bit-identical (double-precision history), observables to 
\begin_inset Formula $10^{-8}$
\end_inset

, all regression tests unchanged; order 1 reaches the same fixed point (
\begin_inset Formula $10^{-13}$
\end_inset

) in about half the steps. The DFTB block reader reproduces the soc_dftb eigenvalues to 
\begin_inset Formula $3\times10^{-6}$
\end_inset

 eV, its order-0 current agrees with an independent Landauer calculation to 10 digits, and 
\begin_inset Flex Code
status collapsed

\begin_layout Plain Layout
populations_atoms.dat
\end_layout

\end_inset

 (including 
\begin_inset Formula $\langle\mathbf{L}\rangle$
\end_inset

) agrees with an independent NEGF calculation to 
\begin_inset Formula $4\times10^{-13}$
\end_inset

.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Section
Known limitations
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize
Perturbation theory in 
\begin_inset Formula $U$
\end_inset

 up to second order;
 large 
\begin_inset Formula $U/|t|$
\end_inset

 may not converge or may converge to the unphysical solutions that the sanity checks reject.
 
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize
Wide-band leads, diagonal in orbital and spin, on chosen contact atoms; the bias is applied to the left lead.
\end_layout


\begin_layout Itemize
The energy grid is uniform;
 resolving sharp resonances needs a small 
\begin_inset Flex Code
status collapsed

\begin_layout Plain Layout
delta
\end_layout

\end_inset

 everywhere.
 
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize
Voltages are swept upwards only (
\begin_inset Flex Code
status collapsed

\begin_layout Plain Layout
delv
\end_layout

\end_inset

 
\begin_inset Formula $>0$
\end_inset

).
 
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize
\begin_inset Flex Code
status collapsed

\begin_layout Plain Layout
build_hamiltonian_from_xyz
\end_layout

\end_inset

 keeps the chain connectivity (bonds 
\begin_inset Formula $i$
\end_inset

–
\begin_inset Formula $i{+}1$
\end_inset

,
 SOC 
\begin_inset Formula $i$
\end_inset

–
\begin_inset Formula $i{+}2$
\end_inset

) of the helix.
 
\end_layout
\begin_layout Itemize
Multi-orbital Hamiltonians: intra-orbital 
\begin_inset Formula $U$
\end_inset

 only (no 
\begin_inset Formula $U'$
\end_inset

, 
\begin_inset Formula $J$
\end_inset

 or inter-site interaction). 
\begin_inset Flex Code
status collapsed

\begin_layout Plain Layout
dftb_hs
